{{- /* End-of-life blocks. Data is an eolView. */ -}}

{{define "eol-why" -}}
{{if .Ended}}{{if .Date}}Security updates for {{.Name}} stopped on {{.Date}}{{else}}Security updates for {{.Name}} have stopped{{end}}: newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, are not fixed any more.
{{- else}}Security updates for {{.Name}} stop on {{.Date}}, in {{.DaysLeft}} days. After that, newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, will not be fixed.{{end}}
{{- if .Extended}} Extended support (often paid) is listed until {{.Extended}}.{{end}}
{{- end}}

{{define "eol-upgrade" -}}
{{if .Successor}}Upgrade to a supported release. The newest supported release listed on endoflife.date is {{.Successor}}{{if .SuccessorAt}} (latest version {{.SuccessorAt}}){{end}}.{{else}}Upgrade to a supported release. The vendor's lifecycle page says which releases are supported{{if .Policy}}: {{.Policy}}{{else if .Page}}; see {{.Page}}{{else}}.{{end}}{{end}}
{{- end}}

{{define "eol-email-one" -}}
{{if eq .Kind "due-soon"}}Reminder: nobody has acknowledged this yet, and security updates stop on {{.Date}}.
{{else if eq .Kind "overdue"}}Reminder: nobody has acknowledged this yet, and security updates have stopped.
{{end}}What's affected:
  {{.ProductLine}}
  That is release {{.Release}} on endoflife.date.

Why it matters:
  {{template "eol-why" .}}

What to do{{if not .Ended}} before {{.Date}}{{end}}:
  1. {{template "eol-upgrade" .}}
  2. Until you can upgrade, limit who can reach it (for example, no access from the internet) and keep an eye on its vendor's advisories.

Links:
{{if .Page}}  endoflife.date: {{.Page}}
{{end}}{{if .Policy}}  Vendor lifecycle: {{.Policy}}
{{end}}{{end}}

{{define "eol-chat-one" -}}
{{if eq .Kind "due-soon"}}Reminder: nobody has acknowledged this yet.
{{else if eq .Kind "overdue"}}Reminder: nobody has acknowledged this yet.
{{end}}{{template "eol-why" .}}
Affects: {{.ProductLine}} (release {{.Release}} on endoflife.date).
What to do: {{template "eol-upgrade" .}}
Until you can upgrade, limit who can reach it.
{{if .Page}}endoflife.date: {{.Page}}
{{end}}When you have dealt with it, run: patchtacio ack {{.AckID}}
{{- end}}

{{define "eol-entry" -}}
{{.Headline}}
   {{template "eol-why" .}}
   What to do: {{template "eol-upgrade" .}}
   Acknowledge with: patchtacio ack {{.AckID}}
{{end}}
